Dashboard r06_claude_canvas_a1 {
  title: 'Marketing Funnel: Traffic Sources'
  description: 'Where website sessions come from and how well each traffic source converts to a purchase.'

  block title: TextBlock {
    content: @md # Marketing Funnel: Traffic Sources ;;
  }

  block headline: VizBlock {
    label: 'Headline'
    settings {
      hide_label: true
    }
    viz: MarkdownViz {
      dataset: thelook
      calculation total_sessions {
        label: 'Sessions'
        formula: @aql sessions ;;
        calc_type: 'measure'
        data_type: 'number'
      }
      calculation conversion_rate {
        label: 'Conversion Rate'
        formula: @aql purchase_conversion_rate ;;
        calc_type: 'measure'
        data_type: 'number'
      }
      values: [
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: 'total_sessions'
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: '#,###0'
          }
        },
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: 'conversion_rate'
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: '#,###0.0%'
          }
        }
      ]
      content: @md
<h2 style="margin: 0; font-weight: 500;">
  The site drew <b>{{ rows[0].values.`Sessions`.formatted }}</b> sessions, and
  <b>{{ rows[0].values.`Conversion Rate`.formatted }}</b> of them ended in a purchase.
</h2>
      ;;
    }
  }

  block v_sessions_by_source: VizBlock {
    label: 'Sessions by Traffic Source'
    viz: BarChart {
      dataset: thelook
      calculation total_sessions {
        label: 'Sessions'
        formula: @aql sessions ;;
        calc_type: 'measure'
        data_type: 'number'
      }
      x_axis: VizFieldFull {
        label: 'Traffic Source'
        ref: r(thelook_events.traffic_source)
        format {
          type: 'text'
        }
      }
      y_axis {
        series {
          field: VizFieldFull {
            ref: 'total_sessions'
            format {
              type: 'number'
              pattern: '#,###0'
            }
          }
          settings {
            color: '#255DD4'
          }
        }
        settings {
          show_data_label_by: 'value'
        }
      }
      settings {
        sort: LineFamilySort {
          type: 'yaxis'
          field_index: 0
          direction: 'desc'
        }
        legend_label: 'hidden'
        row_limit: 5000
      }
    }
  }

  block t_sessions_commentary: TextBlock {
    content: @md
### Where the traffic comes from

- **Email is the biggest driver** of sessions, followed by Adwords. Together they bring in about three quarters of all traffic.
- Facebook and YouTube bring in similar, mid-sized volumes.
- **Organic is the smallest source**, at roughly half the volume of either social channel.

**So what:** traffic depends on two channels, so a slowdown in email or paid search would hit total sessions harder than anything else.
    ;;
  }

  block v_conversion_by_source: VizBlock {
    label: 'Purchase Conversion Rate by Traffic Source'
    viz: BarChart {
      dataset: thelook
      calculation conversion_rate {
        label: 'Conversion Rate'
        formula: @aql purchase_conversion_rate ;;
        calc_type: 'measure'
        data_type: 'number'
      }
      x_axis: VizFieldFull {
        label: 'Traffic Source'
        ref: r(thelook_events.traffic_source)
        format {
          type: 'text'
        }
      }
      y_axis {
        series {
          field: VizFieldFull {
            ref: 'conversion_rate'
            format {
              type: 'number'
              pattern: '#,###0.0%'
            }
          }
          settings {
            color: '#18A59E'
          }
        }
        settings {
          show_data_label_by: 'value'
        }
      }
      settings {
        sort: LineFamilySort {
          type: 'yaxis'
          field_index: 0
          direction: 'desc'
        }
        legend_label: 'hidden'
        row_limit: 5000
      }
    }
  }

  block t_conversion_commentary: TextBlock {
    content: @md
### How well each source converts

- Conversion is **almost identical across channels**: every source sits in a band of about half a percentage point, between 26% and 27%.
- Organic and Facebook convert marginally best, but they bring in the fewest sessions.
- Email and Adwords are at the bottom of the band. The gap is too small to matter.

**So what:** channels differ in *volume*, not *quality*. Growth comes from scaling traffic in the channels we have, not from shifting the mix.
    ;;
  }

  view: CanvasLayout {
    label: 'View 1'
    width: 1200
    height: 980
    grid_size: 20
    auto_expand_vertically: true
    block title {
      position: pos(20, 20, 1160, 60)
    }
    block headline {
      position: pos(20, 80, 1160, 100)
    }
    block v_sessions_by_source {
      position: pos(20, 200, 740, 360)
    }
    block t_sessions_commentary {
      position: pos(780, 200, 400, 360)
    }
    block v_conversion_by_source {
      position: pos(20, 580, 740, 360)
    }
    block t_conversion_commentary {
      position: pos(780, 580, 400, 360)
    }
    mobile {
      mode: 'auto'
    }
  }

  theme: H.themes.vanilla
}
